---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Websites for Insurance Agents | Couch & Craft"
description: "Websites for independent insurance agents that show where you're licensed and make it easy to ask for a quote."
crumb: "Websites for Insurance Agents"
---
{%- set nate = site.work | findBySlug("nate-hall-insurance") -%}
<section class="page-hero band--navy" aria-labelledby="page-heading">
  <div class="container page-hero__inner flow">
    <p class="eyebrow">For independent agents</p>
    <h1 id="page-heading">Websites for independent insurance agents.</h1>
    <p class="page-hero__sub">People shopping for coverage want to know who you are, where you're licensed and how to reach you. Your site should answer all of it before they have to ask.</p>
    <p class="hero__actions">
      <a class="button button--gold" href="/start/" data-track="cta_click" data-label="insurance-hero">Start a project</a>
      <a class="button button--secondary" href="/work/{{ nate.slug }}/">See {{ nate.client }}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="needs-heading">
  <div class="container agent-needs">
    <h2 id="needs-heading">What an agent's site needs that most don't have</h2>
    <dl class="agent-needs__grid">
      <div><dt>Where you're licensed</dt><dd>List the states. Someone two states over shouldn't have to call to find out you can't help them.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Carrier-neutral wording</dt><dd>If you're independent, the site should say so, and shouldn't read like one carrier's brochure.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>A compliance footer</dt><dd>A short, plain disclaimer on every page. Your carriers and your state set the rules. The site just has to follow them.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>A quote form that stays out of health details</dt><dd>Ask what kind of coverage and how to reach them. Keep medical history and policy numbers out of a web form.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--white" aria-labelledby="anatomy-heading">
  <div class="container flow" style="--flow-space: var(--space-l)">
    <div class="flow">
      <h2 id="anatomy-heading">Anatomy of {{ nate.liveUrl | hostname }}</h2>
      <p>{{ nate.client }} is an independent agency in {{ nate.location }}. Here's what's on the site, and why it's there.</p>
    </div>
    {% set annotation = annotations["nate-anatomy-hero"] %}{% set pinsSizes = "(min-width: 1280px) 76rem, 100vw" %}
    {% include "partials/pins.njk" %}
    <div class="anatomy-pair">
      {% set annotation = annotations["nate-anatomy-footer"] %}{% set pinsSizes = "(min-width: 1024px) 44rem, 100vw" %}
      {% include "partials/pins.njk" %}
      <div class="anatomy-pair__form">
        {% set annotation = annotations["nate-anatomy-form"] %}{% set pinsSizes = "(min-width: 1024px) 22rem, 90vw" %}
        {% include "partials/pins.njk" %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="/work/{{ nate.slug }}/">Read the {{ nate.client }} story</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="band">
  <div class="container">
    {%- set faqs = [
      { q: "Can you write the compliance wording for me?", a: "<p>No. That has to come from you, your carriers or your compliance contact. I'll make sure it's on every page and easy to read.</p>" },
      { q: "Will the quote form be safe for health questions?", a: "<p>The form is built to avoid them. It asks what kind of coverage someone wants and how to reach them, and tells them not to send health details or policy numbers.</p>" },
      { q: "What does it cost?", a: ("<p>Websites start at " + (site.pricing.foundationFrom | open) + ". <a href=\"/pricing/\">See the full pricing</a>.</p>") if ready.pricing else null }
    ] -%}
    {% set faqId = "insurance-faq" %}
    {% include "partials/faq.njk" %}
  </div>
</div>

<section class="band band--white related" aria-label="Keep reading">
  <div class="container related__inner">
    <a class="related__link" href="/web-design/">How I build websites</a>
    <a class="related__link" href="/marketing/">Show up on Google Maps</a>
    <a class="related__link" href="/work/">See the sites I've built</a>
  </div>
</section>
